    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier so it activates when the created owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members, while preserving the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n\nThe design mirrors the codebase's established pattern for `namesakeCount`: a create-time snapshot stored on the entity, with the tier derived purely from entity fields in one place.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field with getter/setter (and `toString`), alongside the existing `namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **Schemas** \u2014 added `household_member_count INTEGER` to all four dialects (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **`CountHouseholdMembers`** (new create-flow function) \u2014 mirrors `CountNamesakes`: counts existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` and adds one for the owner being created (a null-household owner is a household of one). Runs after `assignHousehold` has stamped the shared id.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a `countHousehold` step between `countNamesakes` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 the single tier-computation method now returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic. Added `householdMemberCount` to the `ignore` mappings on both `toOwner` overloads (it's internal, not an API input).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe tier logic stays consolidated in `membershipTier(Owner)`, and the household count reuses the existing snapshot-during-create idiom rather than duplicating counting logic in the responders. The `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
